        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "doctor(memory): surface FTS5 unavailable state in doctor checks",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #62328. `openclaw doctor` could report memory embeddings as ready while SQLite FTS5 keyword/BM25 fallback was unavailable in the running gateway, leaving operators without a visible diagnosis.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Extend `doctor.memory.status` with validated `fts` fields (`enabled`, `available`, and optional `error`).\n- Carry the gateway FTS probe through `probeGatewayMemoryStatus`.\n- Warn from `noteMemorySearchHealth` when the gateway reports FTS unavailable.\n- Keep malformed gateway FTS payloads out of the typed doctor response.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Targeted gateway handler coverage verifies valid FTS state is returned and malformed state is ignored.\n- Targeted doctor coverage verifies unavailable FTS5 produces an operator warning, available FTS does not warn, and explicitly disabled memory search keeps its existing early exit.\n- The repaired aggregate diff is limited to the doctor gateway-health, memory-search, and gateway doctor RPC surfaces plus focused tests.\n- Clownfish validation and review completed successfully on head `5a7b237c2f155584d36204119d612f252ee01070`.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `pnpm test:serial src/commands/doctor-gateway-health.test.ts src/commands/doctor-memory-search.test.ts src/gateway/server-methods/doctor.test.ts`\n- `pnpm check:changed`\n\nRequired GitHub checks must be green before merge.",
